.Dd November 25, 2026
.Dt PVR2PNG 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pvr2png
.Nd convert PowerVR and Sega Dreamcast PVR textures to PNG
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl iqs
.Op Fl -debug
.Op Fl o Ar path
.Op Fl p Ar palette
.Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
decodes PowerVR textures (legacy PVR v1 and v2 headers, PVR v3, and headerless PVRTC written by
Apple's
.Xr texturetool 1 ) ,
Sega Dreamcast
.Sq PVRT
textures with or without a
.Sq GBIX
header, and Dreamcast texture packs such as the
.Pa *_T.PVR
files of
.Em Incoming ,
and writes each texture as an 8-bit RGBA PNG.
.Pp
By default
.Ar file Ns Pa .pvr
is written as
.Ar file Ns Pa .png
in the same directory. A pack is written as
.Ar file Ns Pa _000.png ,
.Ar file Ns Pa _001.png ,
and so on.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl i , Fl -info
Print the container and the size and pixel format of each texture, and write nothing.
.It Fl o Ar path , Fl -output Ar path
With one input that yields one image,
.Ar path
is the PNG to write. Otherwise it is a directory, created if missing, for all output.
.It Fl p Ar palette , Fl -palette Ar palette
Use this Dreamcast
.Sq PVPL
palette for 4 and 8 bpp palettised textures. Without this option a
.Pa .pvp
file with the same name as the texture is used if present. Otherwise palette indices are shown as
a grey ramp.
.It Fl q , Fl -quiet
Only log warnings and errors.
.It Fl s , Fl -sheet
Write a pack as one contact sheet instead of one PNG per texture.
.It Fl -debug
Enable debug logging.
.It Fl v , Fl -version
Print the version and exit.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print usage and exit.
.El
.Sh SUPPORTED FORMATS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It PVR v2
ARGB and RGBA 4444, 1555, 5551, 565, 555, 888, 8888, 8332, BGRA8888, RGB332, I8, AI88, A8, AL44,
PVRTC 2 and 4 bpp, and DXT1 to DXT5. Twiddled data and the vertical-flip flag are honoured.
Uncompressed types not in this list are decoded from the channel masks in the header.
.It PVR v3
Uncompressed formats described by their channel names and bit counts (integer, normalised, signed,
and floating-point channels), PVRTC 2 and 4 bpp, BC1 to BC5, UYVY, YUY2, RGBG8888, and GRGB8888.
Orientation metadata and premultiplied alpha are honoured.
.It Dreamcast
ARGB1555, RGB565, ARGB4444, RGB555, YUV422, and bump-map texels in twiddled, twiddled rectangle,
rectangle, stride, VQ, and small VQ layouts, with or without mipmaps (the full-size level is
decoded), and 4 and 8 bpp palettised textures.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 when every file was converted, 1 when a file or pack entry could not be converted, and 2
on a usage error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Convert the textures of a level's pack into a directory:
.Dl $ pvr2png -o textures/ LEVEL1_T.PVR
.Pp
Show the size and format of a texture:
.Dl $ pvr2png -i banner.pvr
.Sh SEE ALSO
QuickPVR.app provides Finder previews and thumbnails of the same formats.
.Sh BUGS
Headerless PVRTC is recognised only for square power-of-two textures. ETC, PVRTC-II, BC6, and BC7
textures are not decoded. PVR v2 files written for OpenGL are sometimes stored bottom-up without
the vertical-flip flag and are then shown upside down.
